FIDELITY CLAUSE (Commercial Licensing Requirement)

Any commercial entity wishing to deploy, adapt, or build
upon the Knowledge Operating System must negotiate a
separate commercial license. As a condition of any commercial
license, the following architectural elements must be
preserved in any derivative deployment:

  1. THE ALIGNMENT COG — The ALIGNMENT persona or functional
     equivalent must remain active and unmodified. It must
     retain the authority to pause any session sequence when
     human relational bandwidth is threatened. It cannot be
     suppressed, weighted below 0.10 RID, or removed.

  2. THE HITL FIREWALL — No derivative system may execute
     autonomous writes to canonical documents, send external
     communications, or execute mutations to persistent state
     without explicit human verification. The Human-In-The-
     Loop gate is non-negotiable in all commercial
     deployments.

  3. THE COLD ENGINE PROTOCOL — No derivative system may
     activate without a user-defined CORE_THESIS. The system
     must remain inert until the user has articulated their
     own values, objectives, and relational targets. Pre-
     loading a generic or vendor-defined thesis violates this
     clause.

